.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPDEL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm groupdel
.Nd delete a group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Ar GROUP
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
removes
.Ar GROUP
from
.Pa /etc/group
(and
.Pa /etc/gshadow
when present).  Refuses to remove a group that is the primary group
of any user in
.Pa /etc/passwd
unless
.Fl f
is given \(em pulling the floor out from under live accounts almost
always orphans something.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Force removal even if
.Ar GROUP
is somebody's primary group.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
Bad usage.
.It 6
.Ar GROUP
does not exist.
.It 8
.Ar GROUP
is the primary group of an existing user (without
.Fl f ) .
.It 10
Failed to update
.Pa /etc/group .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr gshadow 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr groupmod 8 ,
.Xr userdel 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
